From cdbddb86f389bd570cc6a2b8ac91f2fbd2e448b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 23:06:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(upgrade): move beads detector to shared module (a7e1443c
 tombstone)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CI was red on 8 lanes: test/commands/runtime-no-auto-migrate.test.js
pins `migrateCommand.detectBeadsJsonlSource` UNDEFINED (the a7e1443c
implicit-auto-migrate tombstone). Re-exporting that name from the
migrate command revived the identifier and broke Unit Shards 1-3, the
mac/ubuntu Full Matrix, and Coverage.

- lib/beads-detect.js (new): the single, side-effect-free
  detectBeadsJsonlSource() lives in a neutral module, NOT the migrate
  command — so the tombstone stays satisfied (read-only, feeds a
  stderr nudge, writes nothing) and both consumers share ONE detector.
- lib/commands/migrate.js: remove the tombstone-reviving export.
- lib/commands/_issue.js + lib/upgrade-safety.js: both now import the
  shared detector; upgrade-safety drops its duplicated inline scan.
- detector now also finds a split store whose jsonl lives only under
  .beads/backup/ (a layout the migrator itself reads) — the footgun
  no longer survives that layout for either surface.
- upgrade advisory now respects the FORGE_ISSUE_BACKEND env opt-in
  (via resolveIssueBackend), aligning it with the nudge path instead
  of consulting config alone.

Tests added: shared-detector unit (incl. backup layout); stdout is
byte-identical with/without the stderr nudge; a pending migration does
NOT flip upgrade `ok`; env opt-in suppresses the advisory.

Refs: a5399f3d-28df-474e-b5f3-08af6bd7b388

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
